  "notes": "USAGE: Primarily a scientific/technical term used in chemistry, physics, and environmental science. The noun form {沈殿物|ちんでんぶつ} refers to the settled material (sediment/precipitate).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {沈殿物|ちんでんぶつ} (sediment, precipitate)\n- {沈殿|ちんでん}{反応|はんのう} (precipitation reaction)\n- {沈殿|ちんでん}する (to settle, precipitate)\n- {底|そこ}に{沈殿|ちんでん}する (to settle at the bottom)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {堆積|たいせき} (accumulation, sedimentation - geological)\n- {沈澱|ちんでん} (alternative kanji for same word)\n- {浮遊|ふゆう} (floating, suspension - opposite state)",
